      <minutesnonemptyhtmlbody>&lt;div class="WordSection1"&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The Combined Authority
considered its first budget under the Integrated Settlement,
covering 2026/27. &amp;nbsp;It was emphasised that the
&amp;pound;1.25&amp;nbsp;billion budget, the largest to date, would support
transport investment, bus franchising, skills, housing, culture and
net zero programmes. &amp;nbsp;Officers outlined a
&amp;pound;487.3&amp;nbsp;million revenue budget and a
&amp;pound;767&amp;nbsp;million capital programme and noted the use of
one-off reserves to balance transport funding ahead of franchising.
&amp;nbsp;Members thanked the finance team and welcomed clearer budget
presentation, but raised questions about scrutiny time, reserve
levels, inflation risks and future levy pressures. &amp;nbsp;Members
questioned avoiding a mayoral precept and asked for greater
involvement in early budget development. &amp;nbsp;The Chair confirmed
no mayoral precept for 2026/27 and advocated prudent levy use,
noting efforts to keep fares low. &amp;nbsp;Officers advised that
reserves met good practice thresholds and inflation would be
managed within capital allocations. &amp;nbsp;Members supported the
need for clear governance as franchising and settlement reforms
progressed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
